line 8 extra: by-design spec §1.2 arrays are homogeneous, so an array literal's elements must share one type
line 8 type: by-design spec §1.2 arrays are homogeneous, so an array literal's elements must share one type
line 10 type: artifact the type comes from code tsc rejects, and each side's recovery type differs (ours types the rejected literal as its target)
line 11 type: by-design spec §1.3 keeps an array never filled as `never[]`; tsc reports its unobserved declaration as `any[]`. SUB-2101 supports evolving reads after writes, but this case has no writes to infer from.
